# This repo is PUBLIC. Nothing sensitive, and no application source, belongs here.

# Internal working context for Claude Code sessions. Stays on disk so future
# sessions load it; never published. It records strategy, known risks that were
# knowingly accepted, and past defects — all of which are discoverable evidence
# if VoidFlow is ever in a dispute, and none of which a user needs.
CLAUDE.md

# Website source material. Working document for building the site, not part of
# the distribution repo — it carries positioning notes and an explicit list of
# claims that must NOT ship.
CONTEXT.md

# Agent working state. Subagents run with this repo as their working directory
# even when the code they are reviewing lives in the private source repo, so
# their notes land here — and those notes are review findings, defect lists and
# source-tree paths. Same reasoning as CLAUDE.md above: useful on disk, not
# something to hand a reader of the public repo.
.claude/

# Build artifacts — releases are attached to GitHub Releases, never committed
*.app/
*.dmg
*.zip
dist/

# Secrets — notarization credentials, Stripe keys, signing material
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.p12
*.cer
*.provisionprofile

# macOS
.DS_Store
